# Root-level env file -- for Phase 6's repo-root `docker-compose-local.yml` (`env_file: .env`
# feeding the observatory-ws container), not for local non-Docker dev. `npm run start:ws` (this
# root package.json delegating `--prefix observatory-ws`) chdirs into observatory-ws/ before the
# script runs, so @nestjs/config's default cwd-relative lookup finds observatory-ws/.env there,
# not this one -- copy this file for local dev too, but into observatory-ws/.env, matching that
# folder's own .env.example (kept identical to this one; update both if either changes).
# `observatory-ui` needs no env vars at runtime -- it's a static build that talks to the backend
# same-origin through nginx's /api/ proxy (see observatory-ui/nginx.conf).
#
# Every value is validated at boot (observatory-ws/src/config/env.validation.ts); a missing or
# malformed one fails startup immediately, naming the bad variable, rather than failing later on
# the first request that needs it.

# Mongo connection. Placeholder only -- set the real host in your own .env, which is gitignored.
# For local development this is the database server reachable over your network or VPN; in a
# server deployment it is the MongoDB host that deployment provides. The database and collection
# names below are the real ones and should not need changing.
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://mongodb-host:27017
# Self-contained local stack: uncomment this instead, and start with
#   docker compose -f docker-compose-local.yml --profile offline up --build
# which runs a throwaway MongoDB seeded with the 200-record sample fixture. No network access to
# any real database needed.
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb://mongo:27017
#
# A MongoDB running on your own machine (not in Compose) is reachable as:
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb://host.docker.internal:27017
MONGODB_DB=dome_observatory
MONGODB_COLLECTION=Content

PORT=3000

# Restricts CORS to the frontend origin. In both the Docker and bare-metal deployment, nginx
# proxies /api/* same-origin so the browser never actually needs CORS -- this only matters for
# `npm run start:ws` against `ng serve` when observatory-ui's proxy.conf.json isn't in play, or a
# future split-host deployment. Never leave this as '*' in production.
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:4200

# Cap on how long any single Mongo query is allowed to run (maxTimeMS) before the API fails that
# request fast rather than holding a connection open on a shared host. See
# observatory-ws/src/records/records.query.ts.
MONGO_MAX_TIME_MS=5000

# Separate, larger budget applied only to a free-text search (q=...). A rare term or author
# surname is a genuine ~10s query on the MongoDB server's unindexed collection -- measured "Tosatto" at 10.0s.
# See observatory-ws/src/records/records.service.ts's fetchPage.
MONGO_SEARCH_MAX_TIME_MS=20000

# Budget for one /api/export chunk (up to 1000 documents), separate from the two above because it
# is a much larger read than a 25-row search page. See observatory-ws/src/export/export.service.ts.
MONGO_EXPORT_MAX_TIME_MS=30000

# Request rate limits, per client IP over a rolling minute. One budget across all endpoints (not
# one per endpoint -- see observatory-ws/src/common/ip-throttler.guard.ts), with /api/export given
# its own separate, smaller budget because each of those requests returns up to 1000 records.
# Both are optional; these are the defaults. They are an abuse backstop on a shared database host,
# not a ration -- raise them if the hosting deployment can carry more. Every published limit
# (README.md, swagger.ts, the /download/api page) quotes these numbers, so changing one here means
# updating those too.
RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=1200
EXPORT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=60

# Target for `npm run deploy-prod-quick`, an rsync destination for the built frontend. Not read by
# the service and not set by default: the script exits with a message rather than deploying
# somewhere unintended. Export it from your shell rather than committing a value here.
# DEPLOY_TARGET=user@host:/var/www/dome-ml-observatory/dist/

# Matomo, the lab's self-hosted analytics. All four are optional and the whole integration is
# INERT unless MATOMO_TOKEN is set, which is the shipped default: no tracker is constructed and no
# host is contacted. See ROADMAP.md §1 for how to turn it on.
#
# MATOMO_TOKEN is the ONLY credential this service has. Never commit it -- supply it through the
# deployment environment, or a GitHub Actions secret if CI ever needs it. It is required for the
# client IP to be honoured; without it Matomo attributes every API hit to this server instead of
# the caller, which is worse than no data at all.
# MATOMO_URL=https://matomo.biocomputingup.it/matomo.php
# MATOMO_SITE_ID=
# MATOMO_TOKEN=
# MATOMO_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://observatory.dome-ml.org
